Package: bugtool-collector
Version: 0.1.1
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: eveane <https://github.com/eveane/XCP-ng-toolbox>
Depends: openssh-client
Recommends: sshpass
Description: Collect xen-bugtool archives from every host of an XCP-ng pool
 bugtool-collector runs xen-bugtool on every host of an XCP-ng pool over
 SSH, downloads the bundles in parallel (-j N, default 3, 0 = all at once)
 and packs them into one "<pool name or master IP>-<UTC date-time>.tar.gz"
 archive. Installed as /usr/bin/bugtool-collector.
 .
 With no argument, the pool is auto-detected from the XO server database
 (xo-server-db ls server): a single registered pool is collected directly,
 several pools are listed for interactive selection, and the SSH password is
 read from the chosen server entry. Without sshpass, OpenSSH SSH_ASKPASS is
 used, so no extra package is needed. bash/coreutils/grep/tar are
 Essential/required on Debian and are therefore not dependencies.
 .
 For offline (airgapped) XOAs, a self-contained airgap bundle
 (bugtool-collector_<version>_airgap.tar.gz) ships this package plus all
 dependency .debs and an install.sh that runs dpkg -i locally.
Homepage: https://github.com/eveane/XCP-ng-toolbox
